/T (\376\377\000p\0003\000\137\000t\0005\0008\000\137\0003\0005\000\133\0000\000\135)
/TU (Total Living Expenses \050Amounts reported in U\056S\056 dollars\051\056 36\056 Expense Items\056 Expenses not generally allowed\072 We generally do not allow tuition for private schools\054 public or private college expenses\054 charitable contributions\054 voluntary retirement contributions or payments on unsecured debts\056 However\054 we may allow the expenses if proven that they are necessary for the health and welfare of the individual or family or the production of income\056 See Publication 1854 for exceptions\056 Food\054 Clothing and Misc\056 Food\054 Clothing and Miscellaneous\072 Total of food\054 clothing\054 housekeeping supplies\054 and personal care products for one month\056 The miscellaneous allowance is for expenses incurred that are not included in any other allowable living expense items\056 Examples are credit card payments\054 bank fees and charges\054 reading material\054 and school supplies\056 Actual Monthly\056 \044\056)
/Type /Annot
